WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.710
In the first season of Game of Thrones, and
in the first book, Daenerys Targaryen walks

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:12.400
into a big fire, and comes out unharmed. Before
that, she says “fire cannot kill a dragon”.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.920
This has led a lot of people to believe that
Dany, or all Targaryens, cannot be hurt by

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.240
fire. And this is not true. So, a bunch of Targaryens have been burned.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:28.240
Dany’s brother was killed with molten gold.
Aerion Targaryen died after drinking wildfire.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.020
Aegon V Targaryen and Duncan Targaryen died
in a fire at the Tragedy of Summerhall, though

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:39.040
we don’t know exactly what happened there.
And another Targaryen who is burned is Daenerys. Without

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.470
spoiling anything, in a chapter of A Dance
With Dragons, Dany is burned, leaving "Her

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:48.210
skin … pink and tender, [with] pale milky
fluid … leaking from her cracked palms [and]

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:54.270
her burns … healing". Daenerys Targaryen is burned, and is not immune to fire.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.130
If you need any more proof, George R. R. Martin
himself has said several times that Targaryens

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.520
are not immune to fire. Quote: “TARGARYENS
ARE NOT IMMUNE TO FIRE!” Capslock his. “The

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.439
birth of Dany's dragons was unique, magical,
wonderous, a miracle”.

00:01:06.439 --> 00:01:10.829
Another quote: “some fans are reading too
much into the scene in GAME OF THRONES where

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:14.939
the dragons are born … it was never the
case that all Targaryens are immune to all

00:01:14.939 --> 00:01:19.060
fire at all times.”
One more – “no Targaryans are immune to

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.810
fire. The thing with Dany and the dragons,
that was just a one-time magical event, very

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:29.259
special and unique. The Targaryans can tolerate
a bit more heat than most ordinary people,

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:33.039
they like really hot baths and things like
that, but that doesn't mean they're totally

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:37.850
immune to fire”.
So, case closed, yeah? Targaryens are a little

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:41.890
heat-resistant – which explains why Dany
wasn’t burned by this bath, or this egg

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.909
– but the thing on the pyre was a one-off
and Targaryens are not immune to fire.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:53.350
This has implications for R+L=J. Jon Snow
burns his hand at one point, and some people

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:57.959
take this to mean Jon can’t be the son of
Rhaegar Targaryen. But since Targaryens are

00:01:57.959 --> 00:02:03.249
not immune to fire, Jon can still have the
blood of the dragon even though he was burned.

00:02:03.249 --> 00:02:07.659
So yeah. Just wanted to clear that up, ‘cause
it’s a really common misconception. If people

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:10.259
repeat it, show’m these quotes. Thanks for
watching.

